
# Azure Virtual Machine Creation

## Objective

Create a Linux virtual machine within Microsoft Azure to host the portfolio website.

## Configuration

| Setting | Value |
|----------|----------|
| Cloud Provider | Microsoft Azure |
| Region | Australia East |
| Operating System | Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS |
| Authentication | SSH Key |
| Public IP | Dynamic |
| VM Size | B1s |

## Procedure

1. Logged into Azure Portal.
2. Created a new Resource Group.
3. Selected Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS.
4. Configured VM size.
5. Enabled SSH authentication.
6. Downloaded SSH private key.
7. Created the virtual machine.

## Verification


The VM was successfully deployed and assigned a public IP address
